System Architecture & Engineering Highlights:
---------------------------------------------
1. Modular Architecture & Healthcare Domain Scoping:
   - Engineered around four core clinical workflows:
     * Patient Registration & Management
     * Doctor & Department Management
     * Appointment Booking & Scheduling
     * Billing & Invoices
   - Cleanly structured modular design with complete separation of concerns
     (Schema -> Service -> Controller -> Router).

2. Reliability & Resilience Hardening:
   - Built-in graceful in-memory fallback for Redis caching, rate limiting, and Socket.IO
     ensuring full standalone operational capability without external cache dependencies.
   - Robust timezone normalization enforcing UTC midnight and UTC day-of-week calculations
     to eliminate calendar and scheduling drift.
   - Thread-safe atomic sequence counters (PAT-xxxx, DOC-xxxx, APT-xxxx, INV-xxxx,
     REC-xxxx, NUR-xxxx) preventing race conditions and collision bugs.

3. Appointment & Daily Queue Management:
   - High-throughput atomic per-doctor, per-date daily queue token generator (#1, #2, ...).
   - Database-level partial unique compound indexing guaranteeing zero duplicate slot bookings.
   - Real-time doctor leave window tracking with automated booking blackout protection.
   - Comprehensive administrative staff portal for walk-ins and consultation status updates.

4. Financial Engine & Server-Side Document Generation:
   - Centralized deterministic pure-function invoice engine with strict two-decimal precision.
   - Categorized line items with dynamic recalculation upon modifications.
   - High-fidelity server-side PDF generation using pdf-lib for tax invoices,
     appointment slips, and patient ID cards with strict cryptographic role and ownership validation.

5. Visual Identity & User Experience:
   - Custom-crafted PulseCare HMS design system with responsive medical teal theme,
     dark mode support, Framer Motion transitions, and accessible public landing page.
